{#
  NetworkPolicy for an *arr slice-2 ingress rule. sonarr's, radarr's and prowlarr's own
  policies share this exact structure (podSelector on `app: <name>`, traefik admitted
  unconditionally, a caller matchExpressions list, one TCP port) and differ only in the caller
  list and its per-item comments. Those stay at the call site via `{% call %}` rather than
  being swallowed here. The whole point of the comments is that they differ role to role:
  sonarr annotates every caller, radarr only prowlarr and homepage, and prowlarr only its
  isolation probe's control leg. Do not harmonize the call sites to make them look more alike;
  the macro exists to hold the structure they already share, not to grow the shared surface.

  prowlarr's OTHER policy, networkpolicy-flaresolverr.yaml.j2, is NOT this shape and is NOT
  converted. It fences flaresolverr (podSelector `app: flaresolverr`, one caller
  `app: prowlarr`, no traefik entry, no matchExpressions list, port from
  `prowlarr_k8s_flaresolverr_port`), which is a different subject with a different shape.

  Arguments:
    name  Service/pod `app` label this policy selects, and the NetworkPolicy's own name.
    port  TCP port the caller list is scoped to (`container_item.port` at every call site).

  Call with a body holding the `values:` list — one `- <caller>` line per entry, indented to
  column 18 (the list's own column) with an optional trailing `# comment`, exactly as it reads
  in each caller's own file. Call plain (no `{% call %}`) only for a site with no callers to
  list, which none of the three has.
#}
{% macro arr_networkpolicy(name, port) -%}
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: {{ name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: {{ name }}
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: traefik
        - podSelector:
            matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
{% if caller is defined %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: {{ port }}
{% endmacro %}
